== Step 1: elements of order 3 in PGammaL(3,9) ==
Theory: |PGL(3,9)|=42456960, |PGammaL(3,9)|=84913920.
  (g,f) of order 3 => f=0 (f is a homomorphism to Z/2, field automorphism has order 2).
  In PGL: g^3=lambda*I; cubing is bijective on GF(9)* (gcd(3,8)=1), so g/mu has cube I; x^3-1=(x-1)^3 in char 3,
  so g/mu is unipotent: Jordan type (2,1) [elation] or (3) [regular unipotent], and nothing else.
  h u h^-1 = lambda u' with u,u' unipotent forces lambda=1, so PGL-classes of order-3 elements = GL-classes of unipotents.
  Frobenius preserves Jordan type (rank of g-I), so PGammaL does not merge the two classes.
  elation I+E13: rank(g-I)=1, commutant dim 5, |C_GL|=46656, class size=7280
